SEVENTH HOKAGE — ERA REFORMS
Naruto Uzumaki, Nanadaime Hokage — Office of the Hokage

The Seventh Hokage, once the village's most unpredictable knuckle-headed
ninja and jinchuriki of the Nine-Tails, took office in an age of peace
following the great war. His administration's priorities:

1. Modernization of the village infrastructure while preserving the
   Will of Fire and the memory of those who fell.
2. Continued cooperation among the Five Great Nations; standing joint
   missions with Sunagakure and the allied villages.
3. Investment in the Academy and the next generation of shinobi.
4. Maintenance of the shinobi register and reintegration of former
   adversaries who chose the path of peace.

Naruto Uzumaki achieved his lifelong dream of recognition by the whole
village. His pledge: never abandon a comrade, and never give up. By
order of the Seventh Hokage.
